36	// The pack-badge row: the marks of the packs this repo declares, on a single
37	// line of its README. Adoption seeds it and the repo owns it from there — which
38	// is why the row is gated behind `{ badges: true }` (the CLI's `--badges`, passed
39	// by bootstrap alone) rather than converged like the surfaces around it. A
40	// README belongs to its repo: a nightly that re-derived this row would rewrite a
41	// member's README every time its declaration moved, so the nightly stays out and
42	// a stale row is the repo's to fix (re-run the converge with `--badges`).
